From f4f10ae4bd43a5aa0b012de7358a5379dd993028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:38:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ChopGimp 3.32.0: lot 5 (interface): Satin (chopgimp:satin)
 and Incrustation de motif (chopgimp:pattern-overlay) layer styles as
 subclasses of the stroke sharing its fills, modes, mipmap levels and
 compositing (inside the layer, alpha kept; fill_coverage / fill_margin
 hooks), in the Style de calque window (Photoshop's order), Calque > Style de
 calque actions, own dialogs, new ones placed under the stroke / bevel / inner
 effects (CHOPGIMP_NO_INNER_STYLES); PSD export as ChFX and patternFill with
 the document's patterns (Patt block after the layer info); a tool's plain key
 selects the tool its group shows (CHOPGIMP_NO_GROUP_KEY); width profile kept
 first in the options bar; status bar with the zoom first and document info
 (Doc sizes, dimensions, profile, resolution, layers, active tool;
 CHOPGIMP_CLASSIC_STATUSBAR); Photoshop-like document tabs (name @ zoom
 (layer, mode/bits)*, close button on every tab; CHOPGIMP_CLASSIC_TABS)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
